      en: "Isla Catalinita is a small uninhabited island located about 2 km off the southern coast of the Dominican Republic in La Romana province. Covering 1.5 km², it is part of Cotubanamá National Park. The island is surrounded by coral reefs and is a critical nesting site for loggerhead (Caretta caretta) and green sea turtles (Chelonia mydas). Vegetation is dry scrub and coconut palms. Historically used for salt production, it is now a popular destination for boat tours and snorkeling. Water depth around the island rarely exceeds 5 meters. The island is also a bird sanctuary, with species such as the brown pelican and magnificent frigatebird.",
