      en: "Samaná Bay (Bahía de Samaná) is a large bay on the northeastern coast of the Dominican Republic, approximately 45 km long, stretching from the Samaná Peninsula to the town of Sánchez. It is world-famous for the annual humpback whale (Megaptera novaeangliae) migration, with peak season from January to March. The bay features extensive seagrass beds and mangrove forests. Maximum depth is about 35 m. It is a productive fishing ground for tuna and mahi-mahi. Key towns on the bay include Las Terrenas and El Limón. The bay borders Los Haitises National Park. Winter water temperature averages 26 °C. Whale watching is a major tourist activity, with over 3,000 whales visiting annually.",
