      en: "Nalga de Maco National Park in northwestern Dominican Republic spans 536 km² across three provinces. Established in 2002, it protects the watershed of the Río Artibonito, the longest river on Hispaniola. The park's highest point, Pico Nalga de Maco, reaches 1,400 m. It harbors the endemic Hispaniolan parrot (Amazona ventralis) and the Hispaniolan boa (Epicrates striatus). The park's cloud forests support a high diversity of orchids and ferns. Annual rainfall ranges from 1,500 to 2,000 mm. Access is difficult, primarily by hiking or 4x4 vehicles. The park is also home to the vulnerable Hispaniolan solenodon (Solenodon paradoxus).",
