      en: "Playa Rincón is a beach on the northern coast of the Samaná Peninsula, approximately 3 km long. It features fine white sand fringed by coconut palms and is protected by an offshore coral reef that keeps waters calm. Average water temperature is 27 °C. The beach lies within the buffer zone of Los Haitises National Park. It has minimal tourist development. The Río Rincón flows into the sea nearby. The beach is a significant nesting site for sea turtles, including hawksbill and leatherback. Surrounding vegetation is dry forest. The beach is accessible via a rough road from the town of El Limón.",
